<!-- LESSON START -->
<main id="lesson">

  <!-- === SECTION 1: WELCOME & SCARCITY === -->
  <section class="section reveal" data-section="1">
    <span class="section-tag">CHAPTER 1</span>
    <h2>Welcome, Welcome! <span class="accent">Yes Yes!</span></h2>

    <div class="dialogue" data-dialogue="d1">
      <div class="dialogue-avatar"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Tom Nook"></div>
      <div class="dialogue-body">
        <div class="dialogue-name">TOM NOOK</div>
        <div class="dialogue-text" data-text="Ah, hello there, my favorite future investor! Tom Nook here, reporting for educational duty, hm?"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>You may know me as a shopkeeper, a home builder, an occasional banker, an unofficial mayor, and a full-time raccoon. But today I am also something of an <strong>economics enthusiast</strong>.</p>

    <p>So what <em>is</em> economics?</p>

    <p>Economics is the study of how people use their limited resources to meet unlimited wants. In other words, everybody wants lots of things (cozy homes, cool tools, a thriving island) but we only have so many <strong>bells</strong>, so much <strong>time</strong>, and so many <strong>materials</strong>.</p>

    <p>This challenge has a name. We call it <a class="kw" data-kw="scarcity">scarcity</a>.</p>

    <div class="dialogue" data-dialogue="d2">
      <div class="dialogue-avatar"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Tom Nook"></div>
      <div class="dialogue-body">
        <div class="dialogue-name">TOM NOOK</div>
        <div class="dialogue-text" data-text="You have seen scarcity on your island, yes? Everyone hunts for iron nuggets, but there are only so many rocks each day. Tragic, tragic!"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="real-world">
      <p>Real countries deal with this too. Chile has huge deposits of <strong>copper</strong>, which the world uses for technology. Countries that do not have enough of a resource must <strong>trade</strong> for it, just like you might trade fruit or fossils with island visitors.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="memory-hook">
      <strong>Stick It in Your Brain</strong>
      Scarcity = "scarce" things are <em>rare</em>. When wants are big but supplies are small, you have scarcity.
    </div>

    <!-- Nook Check -->
    <div class="nook-check" data-check="c1" data-answer="b">
      <div class="nook-check-q">Quick check, hm! Which of these is the best example of scarcity?</div>
      <div class="nook-check-opts">
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="a">Your island has more peaches than anyone could ever eat</button>
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="b">Only a few iron nuggets appear each day, and many villagers need them</button>
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="c">Tom Nook is charging interest on a loan</button>
      </div>
      <div class="nook-feedback"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- === SECTION 2: NEEDS, WANTS, OPPORTUNITY COST === -->
  <section class="section reveal" data-section="2">
    <span class="section-tag">CHAPTER 2</span>
    <h2>Needs, Wants, and <span class="accent">Tricky Choices</span></h2>

    <div class="dialogue" data-dialogue="d3">
      <div class="dialogue-avatar"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Tom Nook"></div>
      <div class="dialogue-body">
        <div class="dialogue-name">TOM NOOK</div>
        <div class="dialogue-text" data-text="Even a raccoon of my refined taste cannot have everything. Shocking, I know!"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>🍎 Needs</h3>
    <p>Things you cannot live without:</p>

    <div class="example-grid">
      <div class="example-card peach">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Food">
        <div class="label">Food</div>
        <div class="sub">fruit, fish, rice</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sea">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Water">
        <div class="label">Water</div>
        <div class="sub">stay hydrated!</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sand">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Shelter">
        <div class="label">Shelter</div>
        <div class="sub">a roof over your head</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--brown); opacity: 0.85; margin-top: 8px;">Plus clothing, yes yes! Your villager can technically walk around in mismatched socks, but I do not recommend it.</p>

    <h3>✨ Wants</h3>
    <p>Things that make life more exciting, but you can live without them:</p>
    <ul style="margin: 10px 0 14px 26px;">
      <li>A room filled entirely with antique furniture</li>
      <li>A giant robot statue (a personal favorite of mine)</li>
      <li>A vacation to a real-world place like Paris</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Because resources are scarce, both villagers and humans must make <strong>choices</strong>. And every choice has a cost. That cost is called <a class="kw" data-kw="opportunity_cost">opportunity cost</a>.</p>

    <div class="dialogue" data-dialogue="d4">
      <div class="dialogue-avatar"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Tom Nook"></div>
      <div class="dialogue-body">
        <div class="dialogue-name">TOM NOOK</div>
        <div class="dialogue-text" data-text="If you spend 98,000 bells on a home upgrade, the cost is not just the bells! You also gave up that fancy harp you were eyeing. That, my young friend, is opportunity cost."></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="real-world">
      <p>In the real world: if someone buys a new bicycle, they might give up the chance to buy a new game console. Both choices have value. Economics helps us pick the choice that gives us the most.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="memory-hook">
      <strong>Stick It in Your Brain</strong>
      Think "Opportunity Lost." Every yes is also a no to something else.
    </div>

    <!-- Nook Check -->
    <div class="nook-check" data-check="c2" data-answer="c">
      <div class="nook-check-q">If you spend your bells on a new fishing rod instead of a new haircut, what is the opportunity cost?</div>
      <div class="nook-check-opts">
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="a">The bells you spent</button>
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="b">The fishing rod</button>
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="c">The haircut you gave up</button>
      </div>
      <div class="nook-feedback"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- === SECTION 3: GOODS, SERVICES, RESOURCES === -->
  <section class="section reveal" data-section="3">
    <span class="section-tag">CHAPTER 3</span>
    <h2>Goods, Services, and <span class="accent">Hard Work</span></h2>

    <p>Every economy, whether a cute island or a giant nation, runs on <a class="kw" data-kw="goods">goods</a> and <a class="kw" data-kw="services">services</a>.</p>

    <h3>📦 Goods</h3>
    <p>Goods are <strong>physical things</strong> you can hold or use.</p>

    <div class="example-grid">
      <div class="example-card peach">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Furniture">
        <div class="label">Furniture</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sea">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Car">
        <div class="label">Cars</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sand">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Tools">
        <div class="label">Tools</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card leaf">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Electronics">
        <div class="label">Electronics</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>🛎 Services</h3>
    <p>Services are <strong>actions people do for others</strong>. Think Kapp&rsquo;n ferry rides, the Able Sisters tailoring, or Blathers assessing your fossils.</p>

    <div class="example-grid">
      <div class="example-card peach">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Barista">
        <div class="label">Barista</div>
        <div class="sub">makes your coffee</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sea">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Builder">
        <div class="label">Builder</div>
        <div class="sub">builds your home</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sand">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Delivery">
        <div class="label">Delivery</div>
        <div class="sub">brings packages</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>🌱 Three Kinds of Resources</h3>
    <p>Both goods and services need <a class="kw" data-kw="resources">resources</a> to be made.</p>

    <div class="example-grid">
      <div class="example-card leaf">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Natural">
        <div class="label">Natural</div>
        <div class="sub">trees, water, minerals</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card peach">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Human">
        <div class="label">Human</div>
        <div class="sub">skills and creativity</div>
      </div>
      <div class="example-card sand">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Capital">
        <div class="label">Capital</div>
        <div class="sub">tools, machines, buildings</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>When villagers work, they earn <a class="kw" data-kw="income">income</a>, paid in bells. When humans work, they earn dollars, yen, or euros.</p>

    <h3>🎯 Specialization</h3>
    <p>Different places get really, really good at different things. We call that <a class="kw" data-kw="specialization">specialization</a>.</p>

    <div class="dialogue" data-dialogue="d5">
      <div class="dialogue-avatar"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Tom Nook"></div>
      <div class="dialogue-body">
        <div class="dialogue-name">TOM NOOK</div>
        <div class="dialogue-text" data-text="Only Apple makes the iPhone, so they set the price. Only your island has those particular pears. If folks want them, congratulations, you are specialized in pears, yes yes!"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="real-world">
      <p>Japan specializes in technology and cars. Brazil specializes in coffee. Kenya specializes in tea. The United States specializes in large-scale agriculture and airplanes. When everyone trades what they make best, everyone gets more variety and better quality.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="memory-hook">
      <strong>Stick It in Your Brain</strong>
      Specialization = "Do what you are best at, trade for the rest." Like a team where everyone plays their position.
    </div>

    <!-- Nook Check -->
    <div class="nook-check" data-check="c3" data-answer="b">
      <div class="nook-check-q">Which one of these is a <em>service</em>, not a good?</div>
      <div class="nook-check-opts">
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="a">A peach</button>
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="b">A doctor giving you a checkup</button>
        <button class="nook-opt" data-val="c">A fishing rod</button>
      </div>
      <div class="nook-feedback"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- === SECTION 4: SUPPLY & DEMAND === -->
  <section class="section reveal" data-section="4">
    <span class="section-tag">CHAPTER 4</span>
    <h2>Supply, Demand, and <span class="accent">Why Prices Wiggle</span></h2>

    <p>Prices do not appear by magic. They are shaped by two big forces: <a class="kw" data-kw="supply">supply</a> and <a class="kw" data-kw="demand">demand</a>.</p>

    <h3>📦 Supply</h3>
    <p>Supply is <strong>how much of something exists or can be made</strong>.</p>
    <ul style="margin: 10px 0 14px 26px;">
      <li>10 stacks of peaches sitting around? Supply is HIGH.</li>
      <li>Only 1 stack of gold nuggets in the whole town? Supply is LOW.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>🙋 Demand</h3>
    <p>Demand is <strong>how much people want something and are willing to pay for it</strong>.</p>
    <ul style="margin: 10px 0 14px 26px;">
      <li>Everyone in the village wants that golden armor suit? Demand is HIGH.</li>
      <li>Nobody wants another sea bass? Demand is, tragically, LOW.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>📈 How Prices Move</h3>
    <div style="background: var(--paper); border: 3px solid var(--brown); border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0; box-shadow: 0 4px 0 var(--shadow-deep);">
      <p style="margin: 6px 0;">⬇ <strong>Low supply</strong> + ⬆ <strong>high demand</strong> = 💰 <strong style="color: var(--berry);">prices RISE</strong></p>
      <p style="margin: 6px 0;">⬆ <strong>High supply</strong> + ⬇ <strong>low demand</strong> = 🪙 <strong style="color: var(--leaf-deep);">prices DROP</strong></p>
